-- title:
--   Cusp section and its translate meet all components mod p
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$, i.e. the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the image of that field of Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that on $L$, and an $A$-algebra structure on $\mathbb{Z}/p$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero (as a `Fact`) whose Laurent series is the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Let $\psi$ be a ring homomorphism from the $j^{-1}$-chart algebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgInf A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L137) — the elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$ — to $A$, retracting the structure map of $A$ and sending each $f$ to the element of $A$ whose image in $L$ is the $q^0$-coefficient of the Laurent series of $f$. Finally let $z$ be a point of the pullback of [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) (the structure morphism of the two-chart model, the pushout of the two chart spectra, to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$) along $\mathrm{Spec}(A \to \mathbb{Z}/p)$, whose image under the first projection is the image under [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιInf A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L233) of the point obtained by pushing the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathbb{Z}/p$ along $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\psi$ followed by $A \to \mathbb{Z}/p$. The conclusion is that there exists an endomorphism $\tau$ of this pullback with $\tau$ followed by the second projection equal to the second projection — that is, an endomorphism over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathbb{Z}/p$ — such that every irreducible component $Z$ of the underlying space of the pullback contains $z$ or contains $\tau$ applied to $z$. The proof visibly discards $\psi$ and the hypotheses describing it and $z$, so the statement is in fact obtained for an arbitrary point $z$ of the fibre.
--
--   In the classical picture the scheme in question is the mod $p$ fibre of a model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a ring containing $\mathbb{Z}_p[\zeta_p]$, the distinguished point $z$ is the reduction of the cusp $\infty$ cut out by the constant-term map of the $j^{-1}$-chart, and $\tau$ plays the role of the Atkin–Lehner involution $w_p$, which exchanges the two components of the fibre; the assertion is that the two points $z$ and $\tau(z)$ together meet every component. It is used in the construction of a section of the fibre whose image lies in a prescribed irreducible component.
